+Status: implementation-team choice; pending at the starter revision, implemented
+October 25, 2026.
 Add JSON export as a small second change. It creates a clear handoff without a
 schema migration or extra service. Export always contains the visitor's entire
 active queue, regardless of the UI filter, and excludes session identifiers.
 The [requirement](export-requirement.md) owns acceptance criteria.
 
+The implementation (Claude-assisted) adds a read-only `GET /api/export` route.
+It copies only `title`, `url` and `read` on the server, so IDs, timestamps and
+the session never leave the Worker. It never sets a cookie or deletes expired
+rows. The browser requests this route on every export instead of reusing its
+filtered list, and downloads only after a successful response.
+
+Sources: [Worker](../src/worker.js), [browser code](../public/app.js),
+[API tests](../tests/worker.test.js).
+
